.Dd November 1, 2026
.Dt TERM.CONF 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm term.conf
.Nd settings of the terminal on the framebuffer
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Pa /etc/term.conf
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Xr term 1
reads this optional file at its start, or the file its
.Fl c
option names.
A file that does not exist leaves every setting at its default.
Each line is
.Li NAME = VALUE ,
blank, or a comment that begins with a hash; blanks around the name and
the value do not count.
A line with an unknown name or a bad value is reported on standard error,
as
.Ql term: FILE:LINE: NAME: what is wrong ,
and skipped.
.Bl -tag -width scrollback
.It Va font
The packed font's absolute path;
.Pa /usr/share/term/unifont.font
by default.
.It Va scale
The font's scale, 1 or 2; 1 by default.
At 1 a cell is 8 by 16 pixels, at 2 it is 16 by 32.
.It Va scrollback
The lines of history kept above the screen, 0 to 100000; 1000 by
default.
.It Va bell
What the bell does:
.Li audible
sounds the PC speaker,
.Li visual
shows the screen in inverse colors for a tenth of a second,
.Li both
does both and
.Li none
neither;
.Li audible
by default.
The speaker has no volume, so the beep is soft by being short and low,
40 ms at 750 Hz, unless the program sets another pitch with
.Ql "ESC [ 10 ; N ]" ,
in hertz, or length with
.Ql "ESC [ 11 ; N ]" ,
in milliseconds, as on Linux's console; a length of 0, or of 2000 or
more, is silent, and either with no N gives the default back.
.El
.Pp
Ctrl+Shift+Page Up and Ctrl+Shift+Page Down in
.Xr term 1
change the scale and write it back as the line
.Li scale = N ,
replacing the file's
.Va scale
line and keeping its others.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# The Lenovo's 1366x768 screen at 85x24 cells, and a silent bell.
scale = 2
scrollback = 5000
bell = none
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr term 1 ,
.Xr ioctl 2
